# crates/crawler participants for the harvesting benchmark
# (compliance/harvest-benchmark-2026-08-27.md). run-harvest-bench.sh appends
# this to the broker:BrokerConfig it generates, which links both resources
# with broker:participant and sets broker:crawlIntervalSecs 5.
#
# Points at the same two new real Eclipse EDC 0.18.0 participant instances
# EDC's own federated-catalog crawler is benchmarked against
# (compliance/harvest-bench/edc-fedcat-runtime/), started via the existing,
# unmodified ../crawler-edc-fixture/run-instance.sh +
# spike.CatalogFixtureExtension mechanism - see
# ../crawler-edc-integration-test.md for that mechanism's own proof.
#
# No broker:credentialProtocol (the default, "none") on either, matching
# every prior benchmark's own documented scope decision (real EDC-side
# DCP/OID4VP is out of scope - see ../benchmark-dcp-2026-08-27.md).
#
# The 5 s interval is short and observable, matching the period this
# benchmark also configures for EDC's own crawler
# (edc.catalog.cache.execution.period.seconds, see
# edc-fedcat-runtime/run-fedcat-crawler.sh) so both systems' background
# harvesting loops re-crawl at comparable frequency during the load-test
# window.
#
# Shape: docs/configuration.md ("Participants and holder").
@prefix broker: <https://catalog-broker.ds-labs.org/ontologies/config#> .

<urn:harvest-bench:d> a broker:Participant ;
    broker:participantId "harvest-d" ;
    broker:participantName "Harvest participant D (3 datasets)" ;
    broker:catalogRequestUrl "http://127.0.0.1:19221/api/dsp/2025-1/catalog/request" .

<urn:harvest-bench:e> a broker:Participant ;
    broker:participantId "harvest-e" ;
    broker:participantName "Harvest participant E (7 datasets)" ;
    broker:catalogRequestUrl "http://127.0.0.1:19321/api/dsp/2025-1/catalog/request" .
